%I A401243 #21 Nov 11 2026 10:11:38
%S A401243 46698887,46698931,46698943,46698997,46752647,46752889,46752917,
%T A401243 46754039,46754053,46754077,46754189,46754563,46754581,46754599,
%U A401243 46754623,46754633,46754651,46754671,46754681,46754693,46755139,46755173,46755307,46755323,46755353,46755403,46755413
%N A401243 Primes p for which pi_{24;5,19}(p) - pi_{24;1,23}(p) = -1, where pi_{m;a,b,...}(x) is the number of primes <= x which are congruent to a or b or ... (mod m).
%C A401243 From _Leandro Hector Gallego_ and _Jianing Song_: (Start)
%C A401243 This sequence is about one of the 21 prime races modulo 24 between cosets of index 4 in (Z/24Z)*; see A401958 for more details. Specifically, here we have H = {1,23} and S = {5,19}, corresponding to T = {chi_8, chi_12}, where chi_d = (d/.) is the Kronecker symbol viewed as a character modulo N = 24.
%C A401243 This sequence gives primes p such that Sum_{primes q<=p} (chi_8(q) + chi_12(q))/2 = 1.
%C A401243 Assuming GRH and LI (see A401958), the set of x with pi_{24;5,19}(x) > pi_{24;1,23}(x) has logarithmic density 0.99690, making the race between {1,23} and {5,19} the 9th most biased among the 21 races of cosets of index 4 in (Z/24Z)*; see the Zenodo preprint below.
%C A401243 Let D(x) = pi_{24;5,19}(x) - pi_{24;1,23}(x). Below x0 = 7*10^12 there are respectively 30659637567, 30659688364, 30659698140, 30659716342, 30659718072, 30659718286, 30659752652, and 30659759379 primes congruent to 1, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17, 19, or 23 modulo 24, giving D(x0) = 44070. There are 2 sign-changing zones giving a total of 363527 terms below x0:
%C A401243   (1) a(1..308) = 46698887-47462167 (there are 2550 primes a(1) <= p <= a(308) such that D(p) < 0, with D(p) reaching a minimum of -21 at p = 46777463);
%C A401243   (2) a(309..363527) = 1298777752271-1393414587041 (there are 1269395430 primes a(309) <= p <= a(363527) such that D(p) < 0, with D(p) reaching a minimum of -16897 at p = 1307688252769).
%C A401243 The total number of primes p <= x0 with D(p) < 0 is 1269397980. (End)
%H A401243 Jianing Song, <a href="/A401243/b401243.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..49451</a>
%H A401243 Leandro Hector Gallego, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24020025">Logarithmic densities of prime number races between the cosets of a subgroup of index 4 modulo 24</a>, preprint, Zenodo, 2026.
%H A401243 Greg Martin and Daniel Fiorilli, <a href="https://personal.math.ubc.ca/~gerg/slides/Chennai-31Aug10.pdf">Prime number races: An asymptotic formula for the densities</a>, Analytic and Combinatorial Number Theory, Institute of Mathematical Sciences, Chennai, India. August 31, 2010.
%H A401243 Greg Martin, <a href="https://personal.math.ubc.ca/~gerg/slides/Canberra-29Nov18.pdf">Prime number races</a>, Pure Math Seminar, UNSW Canberra. November 29, 2018.
%H A401243 Andrey S. Shchebetov, <a href="https://math101.guru/wp-content/uploads/2018/09/01-A3-Presentation-v7.3EN-no.pdf">Testing Chebyshev's bias for prime numbers up to 10^15</a>, EUCYS 2018.
%H A401243 Jianing Song, <a href="/A401243/a401243.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..363527</a> (all terms below 7*10^12).
%H A401243 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chebyshev%27s_bias">Chebyshev's bias</a>.
%o A401243 (PARI) my(k=0); forprime(p=2, 1e11, if(p%24==1||p%24==23, k--); if(p%24==5||p%24==19, k++); if(k==-1, print1(p, ", ")))
%Y A401243 See A401958 for related sequences.
%K A401243 nonn,changed
%O A401243 1,1
%A A401243 _Jianing Song_, Oct 18 2026
